          "path": "/home/katherine/dac/benchmarks/dacomp-de/dacomp-de-impl-017/docs/data_contract.yaml",
          "line": 2130,
          "original_text": "      business_logic: '- Keep applications where applied_at and source_id are present. - Enrich with source_name and source_type via a left join on source_id; if no source match, name/type are NULL. - Derive application_year and application_quarter from applied_at. - Group by source_id, source_name, source_type, application_year, application_quarter. - Aggregations per group: * total_applications: number of application rows. * unique_candidates: count of distinct non-null candidate_id values. * total_hires: applications with status exactly \"hired\" (string match is exact and case-sensitive). * active_applications: applications with status exactly \"active\". * rejected_applications: applications where rejected_at is present. * applications_with_interviews: applications that have at least one scheduled interview linked by application_id; each application counted once regardless of interview count. * avg_process_days: for each application, compute days from applied_at to rejected_at if present, otherwise to last_activity_at; average these durations; applications lacking both end timestamps do not contribute. - Metrics (expressed as percentages from 0 to 100, no rounding): * hire_rate: total_hires divided by total_applications; 0 if total_applications is 0. * interview_rate: applications_with_interviews divided by total_applications; 0 if total_applications is 0. * interview_to_hire_rate: total_hires divided by applications_with_interviews; 0 if no interviewed applications. * rejection_rate: rejected_applications divided by total_applications; 0 if total_applications is 0. - Rankings per year-quarter: * hire_rate_rank: rank by hire_rate descending (ties share rank; gaps allowed). * volume_rank: rank by total_applications descending (ties share rank; gaps allowed). - performance_tier: assign in order—High Performer (hire_rate ≥ 20 and total_applications ≥ 10), Good Performer (hire_rate ≥ 10 and total_applications ≥ 5), High Volume (total_applications ≥ 10), Medium Volume (total_applications ≥ 5), else Low Volume. - efficiency_score: if total_applications > 0, hire_rate + (total_applications ÷ 10); otherwise 0; no rounding. - Exclude groups with total_applications < 1. - Order rows by application_year descending, application_quarter descending, then efficiency_score descending.'\n",
          "association": "同一原文行同时提及列名和 precision/rounding/format/type-conversion 关键词；未判定语句适用范围"
        }
      ],
